From: PengyOS <https://pengyos.catbee.ca>
Subject: [PATCH] configure.in: save CFLAGS before the python header probe

configure.in ends its python-devel probe with

    CFLAGS="$save_CFLAGS"

and at that point `save_CFLAGS` has not been assigned yet - the file's only
assignment is far below, at the stack-hardening block. So the restore sets
CFLAGS to the empty string and every flag the toolchain passed to configure is
discarded: the generated Makefile compiles with no -O2 and no way to pass a
dialect. Under Buildroot 2026.08's gcc 15.3 that is what makes `-std=gnu17`
unpassable, and hplip's K&R-era code then hits C23's implicit-int permerror:

    prnt/hpps/pserror.c:27:10: error: type defaults to 'int' in declaration of 'column' [-Wimplicit-int]

Saving CFLAGS before the probe makes the existing restore do what it reads as.
One added line; the probe's behaviour is untouched, since it overwrites CFLAGS
only to test for python headers and then restores.

Carried on our own recipe (divergence.toml -> hplip-3.26.6-fork).

--- a/configure.in
+++ b/configure.in
@@ -623,6 +623,7 @@
 fi
 
 SAVE_CPPFLAGS="$CPPFLAGS"
+save_CFLAGS="$CFLAGS"
 CFLAGS=`python-config --includes`
 if [ $? -eq 0 ] 
 then
